Example 3. Given period ratio \(a\), find parameters \(m\) (of elliptic integrals and Jacobi's functions of chapter **16**) and \(q\) (of \(d\) functions).

_m_--In both the cases D>0 and D<0, the period ratio is equal to \(K^{\prime}\)(_m_)/_K_(_m_) (see **18.9**). Knowing \(K^{\prime}\)/_K_, if 1<\(K^{\prime}\)/_K_<=3, use Table **17.3** to find \(m\); if \(K^{\prime}\)/_K_<=3, use the method of Example 6 in chapter **17.** An alternative method is to use Table **18.3** to obtain the necessary entries, thence use

\[\begin{array}{l} m = (e_{2} - e_{3})/(e_{1} - e_{3})\mbox{ in case }\Delta > 0,\\ m = {1 2} - 3e_{2}/4H_{2}\mbox{ in case }\Delta < 0. \end{array}\]

